<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22947" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Indus</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἰνδός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>the name of two rivers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The Indus</i>, <i>that empties into
				the Indian Ocean</i>, now <i>Sind</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 2, 52, 130</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 7</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 20,
				23, § 71</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. Tr.
				5, 3, 24 al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A river in Caria</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 28,
				29, § 103</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 38,
				14, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
